<title>UK: Tate pours 4 mln stg into India sugar plant.</title>
<headline>Tate pours 4 mln stg into India sugar plant.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Tate and Lyle Plc said on Tuesday it had invested 4.1 million stg in a 50 percent stake in a new sugar plant at Chilwaria in India.</p>
<p>The sweetener and animal feed producer will partner Simbhaoli Sugar Mills Ltd in the venture.</p>
<p>The plant, which began production in February, was designed to produce 120,000 tonnes of sugar a year in the medium term with an eventual capacity of 300,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
